Changes in Version 2.1

Version 2.1 adds Section 12 (Software Terms). Creative Commons licenses are not designed for software: they do not address source code, distribution of compiled code, network use or patents. From this version on, Software is licensed under Section 12 and the Supplemental Terms instead of CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. The core terms are unchanged for all Content, Software included: attribution; any use that generates money requires a separate written agreement under Section 10.7; derivatives stay under this Agreement; the restrictions in Section 2.2 apply; and patent applications must cite QNFO as prior art. Sections 1.1, 1.2, 3.1, 4, 7.5, 10.3, 10.5, 10.6 and 10.8 and Appendices B to E are updated to match. All other Content is governed as in version 2.0.

Preamble — Values and Purpose

This License is founded on the following principles:

Human Dignity: Respect for the fundamental rights and dignity of all human beings.
Ethical Innovation: Using knowledge and technology in ways that promote the well-being of all sentient beings.
Social Impact: Prioritizing the creation of positive social, environmental, and humanitarian outcomes.
Collective Benefit: Advancing scientific understanding for the shared benefit of humanity.
Anti-Exploitation: Knowledge should not be hoarded, enclosed, or exploited purely for private profit without commensurate public benefit. Sharing and commercialization are not inherently incompatible — but exploitation and hoarding for profit, without clear contribution to the public good, are fundamentally contrary to the purpose of this License.

The QNFO and QWAV ecosystems — encompassing all projects, code, documentation, data, theories, publications, websites, prompts, AI systems, configurations, diagrams, datasets, and associated materials under the QNFO, QWAV, q08, and related namespaces (collectively, the "Content") — are provided primarily for non-commercial research, education, and activities that promote social good and ethical innovation. Commercial use may be permitted under a separate agreement where it demonstrably serves the public good (see Section 10.7).

1. License Grant

1.1 Base License — Creative Commons

This Content, other than Software, is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International License (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0).

Software (as defined in Section 12.1) is licensed under the QNFO Software Terms in Section 12 instead of CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, because Creative Commons licenses are not designed for software. Section 12 carries the same principles (attribution, non-commercial use, share-alike) into terms written for software.

